5)What is a custom field in WordPress?
A custom field is additional metadata attached to a post, page, or custom post type.
For example:
Post Type: team

Title: Rahul Sharma

Custom fields:
designation = Frontend Developer
experience  = 4 years
email       = rahul@example.com


WordPress stores this metadata in the wp_postmeta database table.
The main functions are:
Function	Purpose
get_post_meta()	Retrieve metadata
update_post_meta()	Add or update metadata
add_post_meta()	Add metadata
delete_post_meta()	Delete metadata
